{# ============================================================================
   THE REPORT FLOW — ONE CONTAINER, THE FULL PAGE (the ruled direction A, with
   D's quick-file discipline inside it).

   Filing an incident is the most consequential thing this product asks anybody to
   do, and it gets an ADDRESS of its own: a route survives a reload, a dropped
   connection, a second tab and a pasted link; it prints; and it is the same
   address another module's "file as incident" button already points at. No click
   beside it can throw a half-written report away.

   THE SAME PAGE, WHATEVER THE ENTRY POINT. A filing that arrives carrying a
   source record — another module's hand-off, the register's report control — renders
   the very same page, with the source card riding at its head; a filing from
   nowhere renders it without one. The slide-over drawer this flow used to open
   for a record-borne filing is retired: one container, one set of partials, one
   POST, refused for the same three reasons.
   ========================================================================== #}
{% extends '@UhifadhiIncident/base.html.twig' %}

{# A PAGE SAYS ONLY WHAT IT IS. The shell's document composes the tab title as
   page — place — brand, so naming the area here would print it twice. #}
{% block title %}Report an incident{% endblock %}

{# THE FILE PREVIEW's vocabulary, and ONLY where the card actually has
   photographs to open in it. A sheet linked on a page with nothing to open is a
   request every reader pays for and nobody uses. #}
{% block stylesheets %}
    {{ parent() }}
    {% if sourceFiles is not empty %}
        <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ asset('bundles/uhifadhistorage/preview.css') }}">
    {% endif %}
{% endblock %}

{% block incident_trail_tail %} <a href="{{ path('incident_dashboard', {uuid: area.uuid}) }}">incidents</a> / report{% endblock %}

{# THE FLOW BRINGS ITS OWN HEADING — the page's plate carries its own title, so
   filling the frame's head socket would print the heading twice. #}
{% block incident_page %}
    {{ include('@UhifadhiIncident/report/_page.html.twig', {
        controller: '@uhifadhi/incident-module/incident-report',
        area: area,
        categories: categories,
        prefill: prefill,
        chosen: chosen,
        csrfToken: csrfToken,
        errors: errors,
        createUrl: createUrl,
        cancelUrl: cancelUrl,
        sourceFiles: sourceFiles,
    }, with_context: false) }}
{% endblock %}
